  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Decent work effectively mainstreamed in the agenda and programmes of regional and sub regional partner institutions, including the AU UN, and the AfDB</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Significant progress has been achieved in strengthening partnerships and integrating decent work into regional frameworks, including the systematic mainstreaming of gender equality. However, challenges remain in fully integrating this agenda into the policies and programmes of key institutions. These gaps reduce policy coherence, limit coordinated action and affect the overall impact of efforts to promote employment, social justice, gender equality, and equal treatment and opportunities for all, in line with Agenda 2030 and Agenda 2063.
Building on lessons learned from the 2024&#x2013;2025 biennium, this regional programme supports African constituents in shaping a renewed social contract, including through the 15th African Regional Meeting. It also aims to strengthen engagement with international and regional organizations and financial institutions, such as the African Union Commission, the Economic Commission for Africa, and the African Development Bank. Key expected results include the implementation of strategic partnerships and joint policy initiatives, the dissemination of the Model Law and Toolkit, strengthened uptake of Convention No. 190, and the validation of the Africa Minimum Wage Report by continental bodies. Beneficiaries include parliamentarians, policymakers, labour institutions, as well as workers and employers, who will benefit from stronger and more inclusive protections.</narrative>
  </description>
